{"error":false,"activeTest":false,"task":{"id":14242716,"type":"Review","status":"Processed","importance":1,"reason":null,"locked":null,"proofId":null,"currentQuestionId":null,"currentQuestionTimestamp":null,"progress":1,"points":4,"passed":1,"rawPointsAwarded":2,"pointsAwarded":2,"mp":null,"mpAwarded":null,"mpDecayRate":null,"student":{"id":57976,"firstName":"Thomas","lastName":"Walker","locale":null,"subscriptionId":"sub_1UO4EsD4gcTFRx9701mbmpsi","sequenceId":16},"course":{"id":145,"name":"Mathematics for Machine Learning"},"topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"test":{"id":null,"name":null,"diagnostic":null,"timeLimit":null,"questionCount":null},"created":"2026-10-15T13:29:21.000Z","started":"2026-10-15T13:35:15.000Z","completed":"2026-10-15T13:36:51.000Z","processed":"2026-10-15T13:37:00.000Z","progressStr":"100%","answers":[{"id":62268746,"created":"2026-10-15T13:35:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15898,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:35 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":81404,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":12681,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>$11$ is <strong>not</strong> a prime number, or $15$ is <strong>not</strong> divisible by $5.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$11$ is a prime number}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$15$ is divisible by $5$}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","choice1":"$\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q$","choice2":"$\\neg P \\lor Q$","choice3":"$\\neg (P \\lor  Q)$","choice4":"$\\neg P \\land \\neg Q$","choice5":"$\\neg (\\neg P \\land Q)$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>The sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$11$ is <strong>not</strong> a prime number </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $\\neg P.$ </p>\n<p>The sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$15$ is <strong>not</strong> divisible by $5$ </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $\\neg Q.$</p>\n<p>Therefore, the sentence</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$11$ is <strong>not</strong> a prime number, or $15$ is <strong>not</strong> divisible by $5$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>can be expressed symbolically as $\\neg P \\lor \\neg Q.$</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12681,"title":"Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"},"group":{"id":24446,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242716,"answer":{"id":62268746,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:35:30.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":3,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15898},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62268769,"created":"2026-10-15T13:35:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12145,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:35 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":176858,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12702,"text":"<p>Consider the following statement.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>What is the negation of this statement?</p>\n","choice1":"$-1$ is not greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$","choice2":"$-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$","choice3":"$-\\sqrt{2}$ is not greater than $-1.$","choice4":"$-1$ is  equal to $-\\sqrt{2}.$","choice5":"$-\\sqrt{2}$ is greater than $-1.$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Let&#39;s denote the given statement as $P.$</p>\n<p>The symbol &quot;$\\neg$&quot; represents negation. So, our task is to negate the given sentence. </p>\n<p>To negate our plain English sentence, we place the words &quot;It is not true that&quot; in front of it. This gives the following:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It is not true that $-1$ is greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>In other words, $-1$ is <em>not</em> greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, $\\neg P $ means the following:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$-1$ is <strong>not</strong> greater than $-\\sqrt{2}.$</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Note that $P$ is <strong>true,</strong> while $\\neg P$ is <strong>false.</strong></p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12702,"title":"Negating a Plain English Statement"},"group":{"id":24815,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242716,"answer":{"id":62268769,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:35:46.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12145},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62268815,"created":"2026-10-15T13:36:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12982,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:36 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":176861,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12681,"text":"<blockquote>\n<p>$\\pi$ is <strong>not</strong> a rational or negative number.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Express the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>$P: \\textrm{$\\pi$ is a rational number}$</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>$Q: \\textrm{$\\pi$ is a negative number}$</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n","choice1":"$\\neg (P \\lor Q)$ ","choice2":"$\\neg (P \\land Q)$ ","choice3":"$\\neg P \\lor Q$ ","choice4":"$P \\land \\neg Q$ ","choice5":"$ P \\lor \\neg Q$ ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: </p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>$\\pi$ is a rational or negative number, </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>which can be expressed symbolically as $P\\lor Q.$</p>\n<p>The negation is represented by the symbol &quot;$\\neg$&quot;.  </p>\n<p>Therefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as $\\neg (P\\lor Q).$</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12681,"title":"Expressing a Negated Sentence in Symbolic Form"},"group":{"id":24445,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242716,"answer":{"id":62268815,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:36:02.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":5,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12982},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62268851,"created":"2026-10-15T13:36:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15171,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:36 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":176872,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":12683,"text":"<p>Simplify the statement $\\neg \\left[\\neg\\left(  \\neg(\\neg C)  \\land D\\right)\\right].$ </p>\n","choice1":" $C \\land D$ ","choice2":" $\\neg(C \\land D)$ ","choice3":" $\\neg C \\land D$","choice4":" $\\neg (\\neg C \\land D)$ ","choice5":" $\\neg C \\land \\neg D$ ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Two negations in a row cancel each other out. So, we can simplify $\\neg (\\neg C)$ to $C.$ </p>\n<p>As a result of this, the statement simplifes to </p>\n<p>\\[\n\\neg \\left[\\neg\\left(  C  \\land D\\right)\\right].\n\\]</p>\n<p>Then, we can simplify $\\neg \\left[\\neg\\left(  C  \\land D\\right)\\right]]$ to $ C  \\land D.$</p>\n<p>Therefore, the given statement can be simplified to </p>\n<p>\\[\nC  \\land D.\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12683,"title":"Simplifying a Double Negation"},"group":{"id":24450,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14242716,"answer":{"id":62268851,"cread":"2026-10-15T13:36:22.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15171},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62268888,"created":"2026-10-15T13:36:50.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":null,"freeResponse":"[0,0,0,0]","timeElapsed":23703,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 1:36 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:24","question":{"id":182356,"format":"SS","difficulty":1,"exampleId":12682,"text":"<p> Find the missing values in the following truth table:</p>\n","choice1":" ","choice2":" ","choice3":" ","choice4":" ","choice5":" ","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p><p> First, we add a column for $\\neg A,$ where the truth values are opposite to the corresponding values in the column for $A.$ </p></p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\neg A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n\n<p><p>Then, we add a column for $\\neg  A \\lor B.$ Remember that $\\neg A \\lor B$ is true if either $\\neg A$ is true or $B$ is true. </p></p>\n<table rules=all cellpadding=10 align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,\\neg A \\lor B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm F$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$</td>\n</tr>\n</table>\n","topic":{"id":2790,"name":"The \"Not\" Connective"},"example":{"id":12682,"title":"Completing a Truth Table for a Compound Statement"},"group":{"id":26157,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":{"segments":[{"text":"<table rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"10\" align=\"center\" style=\"border:1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\">\n<tr>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,A\\,$</td>\n    <td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,B\\,$</td>\n<td bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\, \\neg A \\lor B\\,$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center\">"},{"select":{"options":["$\\textrm{T}$","$\\textrm{F}$"],"margin":{"left":18,"right":0,"top":0,"bottom":0},"context":"text","index":0,"selectedIndex":0,"correct":true,"disabled":true}},{"text":"</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n    <td  align=\"center\">$\\textrm T$</td>\n    <td  align=\"center